[size=4]Pick the colour of terminal text, separate from your Pip-Boy. It works with Pip-Boy FX on or off and needs no ini edits.[/size]

[img]{IMG:strip-how-it-works}[/img]

[list]
[*][b]Your colour on every terminal.[/b] Terminal screens, holotapes played in a terminal and the terminal's buttons all use the colour you pick.
[*][b]Pip-Boy FX on or off.[/b] With FX on, the game draws terminals in your Pip-Boy colour, so the mod lends your terminal colour to the Pip-Boy while a terminal is open and puts your own colour back when you leave. With FX off, it tints the terminal screen directly.
[*][b]No more white terminals.[/b] Turning Pip-Boy FX off normally leaves terminal text plain white. Now it keeps a colour.
[/list]

[img]{IMG:terminal}[/img]

[img]{IMG:strip-what-you-get}[/img]

[list]
[*][b]An MCM page.[/b] Presets (Classic green, Amber, White, Blue, Red), red, green and blue sliders, and a live preview of a terminal screen.
[*][b]A settings holotape.[/b] For players without MCM: the same presets and colour steps. It appears once among your holotapes. Play it inside a terminal to see changes as you make them.
[*][b]A light plugin.[/b] ESL-flagged, so it takes no load order slot.
[/list]

[img]{IMG:mcm}[/img]

[img]{IMG:strip-install}[/img]

[list=1]
[*]Install with your mod manager.
[*]The installer asks which version of Fallout 4 you play and marks the right one. Pick it.
[/list]
[b]Needs:[/b] F4SE (0.6.23 for 1.10.163, 0.7.x for later versions), Address Library for F4SE Plugins, and the Microsoft Visual C++ 2015-2022 redistributable (x64). MCM is optional.
[b]Tested on:[/b] OG (1.10.163) and AE (1.11.240). NG (1.10.984): untested.

[img]{IMG:strip-choose-what-it-does}[/img]

In MCM, open [b]Terminal Colors Unlocked[/b]. Or play the [b]Terminal Colors Unlocked Settings[/b] holotape.
[list]
[*][b]Colour terminals:[/b] on or off. Off leaves terminals exactly as the game draws them.
[*][b]Preset:[/b] pick a colour, or Custom to use the sliders.
[*][b]Red, Green, Blue:[/b] 0 to 255 each.
[/list]

[img]{IMG:strip-good-to-know}[/img]

[list]
[*]Not compatible with other mods that change terminal colours. Use one at a time.
[*]With Pip-Boy FX on, your Pip-Boy colour only changes while a terminal is open, and only in memory: your saved settings are never touched.
[*]With Pip-Boy FX on, holotapes played on the Pip-Boy itself keep the Pip-Boy colour.
[*]Changes from MCM show the next time you open a terminal.
[/list]

